OL,3,GNEWSAGuildhall Square turns red and
OL,4,Awhite for Derry City's FAI cup victory
OL,5,
OL,6,FThousands of people have packed into
OL,7,FGuildhall Square to welcome home Derry
OL,8,FCity's footballers following their FAI
OL,9,FCup final triumph.
OL,11,FThe Candystripes secured their seventh
OL,12,FFAI Cup win with a 1-0 victory over
OL,13,FWaterford at the Aviva Stadium in
OL,14,FDublin on Sunday.
OL,16,FA 69th-minute long-range goal from
OL,17,FDarragh Burns, his first in the red and
OL,18,Fwhite of Derry City, was enough to
OL,19,Fsecure a hard-fought victory and edge
OL,20,Fout The Blues in front of almost 37,000
OL,21,Ffans.
OL,23,APub: 09-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
